  - House:Whitlock:Inside
  greetings:
  - Sit anywhere, hon. Coffee's burnt but it's hot.
  - Evening, Detective. You look like you need pie.
  aboutSelf: Thirty-one years behind this counter. My Earl built the place, God rest him. I still wear his ring. Feels rude not to.
  aboutTown: Semblance takes care of its own. We look a little rough around the edges, sure. Something in the water, old Doc Pruitt used to say. Nobody here minds.
  seenAnythingStrange: Strange? Hon, you'll have to narrow that down. ...Fine. Somebody's been eating the pies out of my case at night. Not cutting them. Eating them. With their hands.
  foundersDay: Founders' Day? It rained buckets, so we all crammed into the church hall. I won the pie contest. Again. Cherry.
  gossip:
  - title: About Harlan Hollis
    response: Harlan lost the little finger off his right hand to a baler in '71. Didn't even stop working. Wrapped it in his hanky and finished the row.
  - title: About Father Crane
    response: Father Crane hasn't eaten a bite in here in weeks. Says he's fasting. I say he looks like a coat hanger.
  - title: About Ada Whitlock
    response: My Ada's left eye is green, like her daddy's. That's how I know she's mine.
